  <h3>C R U D</h3>
<p>The acronym CRUD stands for CREATE, READ, UPDATE and DELETE. They describe the four essential operations for creating and managing persistent data elements (data that is permanently stored) in databases.  See the following website to learn more:</p>


  <ul>
      <li><a href="//www.humio.com/glossary/crud/#:~:text=CRUD%20is%20the%20acronym%20for,in%20relational%20and%20NoSQL%20databases." target="_blank" rel="noopener">C R U D <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 28 28"><path d="M22 14.5v5c0 2.484-2.016 4.5-4.5 4.5h-13A4.502 4.502 0 0 1 0 19.5v-13C0 4.016 2.016 2 4.5 2h11c.281 0 .5.219.5.5v1c0 .281-.219.5-.5.5h-11A2.507 2.507 0 0 0 2 6.5v13C2 20.875 3.125 22 4.5 22h13c1.375 0 2.5-1.125 2.5-2.5v-5c0-.281.219-.5.5-.5h1c.281 0 .5.219.5.5zM28 1v8c0 .547-.453 1-1 1a.99.99 0 0 1-.703-.297l-2.75-2.75L13.36 17.14c-.094.094-.234.156-.359.156s-.266-.063-.359-.156l-1.781-1.781c-.094-.094-.156-.234-.156-.359s.063-.266.156-.359L21.048 4.454l-2.75-2.75a.996.996 0 0 1-.297-.703c0-.547.453-1 1-1h8c.547 0 1 .453 1 1z"/></svg></a></li>
